  "body": "Split from issue #1940 (CODE-53 remainder), filed by triage task 12006 (lane code-x, 2026-11-08).\n\n## Problem\nThe mcpx docs explain the server-side `?codemode=false` surface (`pkgs/mcpx/docs/mcp.md`), but a user who wants to opt mcpx out of opencode v2 code-mode wrapping is never shown the `codemode: false` MCP configuration example, and `pkgs/mcpx/docs/plugins.md` still says (verified at origin/main 13ebeccaff12d7f242cc6e29f86f5fcc55fc32fc, ~line 302) that whether v2 code-mode defaults recognise mcpx and turn wrapping off for it is unknown — stale, since the behaviour is now documented and implemented (PLG-35, PR #2992 merged).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `pkgs/mcpx/docs/mcp.md` and/or `pkgs/mcpx/docs/plugins.md` show a concrete `codemode: false` mcpx configuration example for opencode users.\n- The stale unknown caveat in `pkgs/mcpx/docs/plugins.md` is corrected to match the documented behaviour.\n- Docs-only change; no code behaviour changes.\n\nParent: issue #1940. Sibling slice: PLG-38 (filed separately from the same triage).\n",
